From: Harvi654 <202698022+Harvi654@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] comctl32: Paint the themed v6 status bar background only on erase.

AI-assisted (v1 from Autodesk-Inventor-for-Linux, v2 Codex), original
code; LGPL-2.1-or-later. Not submitted upstream.

Windows 10 (MEASURE windows-2026-11-07, x86_64 and i686): a themed v6
status bar paints its background only in WM_ERASEBKGND, so an
application's own erase fill survives WM_PAINT; unthemed v5/v6 controls
always repaint their background in WM_PAINT. SB_SETTEXT erases in v6,
with or without a theme, and does not erase in v5. Owner-drawn parts get
no theme pane over what their owner painted.

Wine painted the background in every WM_PAINT and invalidated without
erasing, so Inventor's dark status bar (its own WM_ERASEBKGND fill) was
painted over in white.

The change is limited to themed v6 (STATUSBAR_HasTheme): classic and v5
painting and the setters' invalidations stay as in vanilla Wine, apart
from the measured v6 SB_SETTEXT erase. Other setters were not measured
and are not changed outside themed v6. The test checks marker pixels
outside the text for normal, borderless and owner-drawn transparent
parts, without font-dependent coordinates.

v2 (2026-11-07): restrict v1's general erase-only painting and erasing
invalidations to themed v6, keep the v6 SB_SETTEXT erase, and add the
Windows-derived test (patches/candidates/comctl32-statusbar-v2).
v2 merged (2026-11-11): v1 and the two incremental v2 stages combined
into this one file for winum-11.20-1; the resulting tree is unchanged.

